      "population": "Trained operators on 3D stereophotogrammetry/clinical landmarking (literature recalled from memory); novice values extrapolated (about 1.3-2x on ambiguous points)",
      "source_urls": [],
      "status": "knowledge",
      "notes": "Engine design defaults, not measurements. Combine sigma = sqrt(sigma_class^2 + sigma_motor^2); motor term 0.5-1 screen px (trained) or 0.7-1.5 screen px (novice) times image px per screen px at placement zoom (about 0.4 mm per screen px at fit-to-window on a 12 MP portrait, negligible at 100% zoom). Huber threshold 2 sigma. Library default user-pin sigma 0.75% IOD (~0.66 mm) matches only the expert crisp-corner row (contested). Expert sigma values in this row are design choices slightly below the trained-error midpoint."
